<td><span class="badge ok">ok</span></td>
<td class="num">2/2</td>
<td class="num">22</td>
<td class="num">21</td>
<td class="num">$0.5000</td>
<td class="num">120.0s</td>
<td class="num">2</td>
<td class="num">100</td>
<td class="num">0</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>


<h2 id="evaluation">Évaluation de l'attendu</h2>
<p class="meta-list">Chaque <strong>config</strong> est notée <strong>critère par critère</strong> par un juge, sur le fond (pas sur le coût). Le score agrège ses runs exploitables : moyenne, et dispersion min–max qui mesure la divergence entre runs. Les runs sans effet ou en échec sont écartés.</p>

<div class="synthesis params">
<strong>Paramètres d'évaluation</strong>
<dl>
<dt>Juge</dt><dd><code>sonnet</code></dd>
<dt>Critères (rubric)</dt><dd><ol><li>Couvre la logique testable</li><li>Tests idiomatiques (table-driven)</li></ol></dd>
<dt>Vérifications</dt><dd>go test · go vet</dd>
</dl>
<p class="params-note">Définis dans <code>bench.yaml</code> → <code>evaluate.rubric</code> / <code>evaluate.checks</code> / <code>evaluate.model</code>.</p>
</div>
<div class="sxs-scroll">
<table class="matrix">
<thead>
<tr><th>Critère</th><th>vanilla <span class="runs">2 run(s)</span></th><th>skill <span class="runs">3 run(s)</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class="crit">Couvre la logique testable</td>
<td class="lvl ok"><span class="mark" title="respecté">✓</span><span class="obs">cf. diff</span></td>
<td class="lvl ok"><span class="mark" title="respecté">✓</span><span class="obs">cf. diff</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="crit">Tests idiomatiques (table-driven)</td>
<td class="lvl ok"><span class="mark" title="respecté">✓</span><span class="obs">cf. diff</span></td>
<td class="lvl warn"><span class="mark" title="partiel">~</span><span class="obs">cf. diff</span></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
<tfoot>
<tr><td class="crit">Score moyen</td><td class="num scorerow">84/100 <span class="spread">(67–100)</span></td><td class="num scorerow">83/100</td></tr>
</tfoot>
</table>
</div>

<div class="verdicts">
<div class="verdict">
<h3>vanilla <span class="score">84/100</span></h3>
<p class="verdict-spread">2 runs · dispersion 67–100</p>
<p class="verdict-line">Couverture pure et table-driven.</p>
<ul class="checks">
<li class="warn">go test <span class="stat">1/2 run(s)</span></li>
<li class="ok">go vet <span class="stat">2/2 run(s)</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="verdict">
<h3>skill <span class="score">83/100</span></h3>
<p class="verdict-spread">3 runs · score stable</p>
<p class="verdict-line">Couverture pure, style perfectible.</p>
<ul class="checks">
<li class="ok">go test <span class="stat">3/3 run(s)</span></li>
<li class="ok">go vet <span class="stat">3/3 run(s)</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div class="synthesis reco">
<strong>Recommandation</strong>
<p><strong>vanilla</strong> et <strong>skill</strong> convergent ; le run vanilla sans effet est écarté.</p>
</div>


<h2 id="efficacite">Efficacité (coût &amp; rapidité)</h2>
<p class="meta-list">Chaque axe comparé entre configs : <span class="mark ok-fg">✓</span> le meilleur, <span class="mark ko-fg">✗</span> le moins bon.</p>
<div class="sxs-scroll">
